<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Qatwan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1141">1141</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Qatwan was fought in 1141 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a>, a Buddhist Sinicised steppe power, defeated the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar">Ahmad Sanjar</a>. The defeat destroyed Seljuk authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. It fatally undermined Sanjar's prestige and contributed to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan.jpg" alt="Battle of Qatwan" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Qatwan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
